.{
    // A008 is a rule aegis declares (its lint_rules, read from the pinned aegis): a reference to
    // one of its targets (std's hand wipe, constant-time comparisons, every key type) reached
    // through each way a name is held, and the same way reaching the answer.
    // A target is a declaration, reached only by a name evaluated as the program compiles; memory
    // a load or store moves holds runtime values, never a name.
    .na = .{.memory},
}
